AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-pq/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A gate may declare one subject chip[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chip[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip: add the generic `presentation.chip` field (glyph, label, optional [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]color), normalize and protect it like `panel_icon`, project it into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notification `action_data`, and add the tolerant zero-I/O reader every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render surface uses.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Frozen task-type presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]freeze[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]freeze: add the module that resolves one task type into a frozen glyph, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]human name, accent, and ordered required-field facts at gate-creation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]time, plus the strict parser, chip projection, note line, and Markdown [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fact every later phase renders from.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The toast and the notification row[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]dense[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dense: give TaskTriage and BeadSnooze their own toast branch with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip, the typed detail line, and warning severity, and render the chip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph on notification rows.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The gate detail pane and the gate review modal[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]detail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]detail: render the declared chip as its own row in the notification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal's gate pane and in the custom gate review modal's header, from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`action_data` only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task bead gates declare their type[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gates[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip, freeze[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates: freeze the task-type display block into the TaskTriage and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BeadSnooze payloads, declare the chip, the typed note line, and the type[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag, add the `**Task type:**` preview fact, and rebuild the whole [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation in kind validation instead of hand-checking its fields.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A pending gate refreshes when its type presentation changes[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]refresh[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gates[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh: fold the frozen display block into the reconciler's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation fingerprint and bump the presentation format version so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pending gates carrying the old, typeless presentation are replaced.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prove it end to end and document it[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prove[dim] · [dim][/dim]after dense, detail, gates, refresh[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prove: add the one end-to-end test that drives a real typed gate through[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every surface, refresh and extend the PNG snapshots, and document the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip field and th